		Thus, on a homogeneous complete network, it is optimal to promote uniformly to all of the population. This result is not obvious, since one could have suggested, e.g., to advertise heavily to one half of the population, and let internal influence effects lead to adoption of the second half. We note, however, that this result is consistent with~\cite{fibich2021diffusion}, where it was shown that networks that are homogeneous in~$p$ exhibit faster diffusion than those which are heterogeneous. 

