Experimental results show that their scheme outperforms centralized Double Deep Q-Learning (DDQN) and further analyze the behavior and information exchange of the agents.

In a different note, Heo et al. in \cite{9236954} propose a Graph Neural Network (GNN) based SFC model, which employs an encoder-decoder architecture.
The encoder extracts a representation of the network topology, while the decoder estimates the probabilities of neighboring nodes processing a VNF.
To support their case, the authors argue that related works with high-level intelligent models such as Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) are not efficient in utilizing the topology information of networks and cannot be applied to dynamically changing topologies, as the models expect a fixed topology.
Their solution outperforms the DNN based baseline model in the conducted experiments.

