Figures \ref{fig:earthquake-reeb} and \ref{fig:mountain-reeb} show an example reconstruction of plate tectonic boundaries and the intercontinental seismic zone, respectively, using the $\alpha$-Reeb graph constriction on epicenters of earthquakes (Figures \ref{fig:earthquake-raw} and \ref{fig:mountain-raw}) available in the global earthquake catalog.
Currently, the $\alpha$-Reeb construction only uses epicenter locations, measured by latitude and longitude (as in Figure \ref{fig:earthquake-raw}). By including features like depth and location error ellipsoids, we predict that our graph reconstruction will be more accurate and useful.

