Image segmentation is a critical enabler for tasks ranging from medical diagnostics to autonomous driving.
However, the correct segmentation semantics --- where are boundaries located? what segments are logically similar? --- change depending on the domain, such that state-of-the-art foundation models can generate meaningless and incorrect results. 
Moreover, in certain domains, fine-tuning and retraining techniques are infeasible:
  obtaining labels is costly and time-consuming;
