\paragraph{Mazda Bechmark Problems:} The implementation is taken from~\citep{kohira2018proposal} (link: \url{https://ladse.eng.isas.jaxa.jp/benchmark/}, license: no license, last accessed: May 1st, 2025). The Mazda problem has two raw forms: a 4-objectives problem 148D (Mazda\_SCA) and a 5-objectives 222D problem (Mazda), and both of them have inequality constraints. For both problems, we equally weight each objective to form a single objective and perform a penalty transform:

\[f_{multiobj\_penalty}(x) = \frac{1}{N}\sum^N_{i=1}f(x) + \rho \sum^C_{j=1} max(0, g_j(x))\]

where $N$ is the number of objectives, $C$ is the number of inequality constraints, and we use $\rho=$ 10 for both variants of Mazda problem. 


