\paragraph{Sub-path-Level Perturbations.}
For sub-path-level perturbations, we remove a sub-path, typically a triplet, from the derived path. Compared to node- and edge-level perturbations, these changes tend to have a greater impact on the reasoning path, as they involve the removal of multiple elements at once.

