\section{Study Design}
\label{sect:study_design}

In this section, we present our research methodology and the study phases, as can be seen in Figure \ref{fig:overview}.

\subsection{Research Questions}

\noindent \textbf{RQ1:} \textit{What PTM-related challenges do downstream developers encounter in software systems?}

Reuse of PTMs comes with its own challenges, spanning both technical limitations and engineering practices \cite{Davis2023}. This research question focuses on identifying and categorizing these challenges to better understand the nature of difficulties downstream developers face in their software systems that reuse PTMs.

% Understanding these challenges is crucial, as they may influence how efficiently developers can address PTM-related issues.

% \noindent \textbf{RQ2:} \textit{How long do downstream developers take to resolve PTM-related issue reports in software system compared to non-PTM-related issues?}

\noindent \textbf{RQ2:} \textit{How does the resolution time of PTM-related issues compare to non-PTM-related issues in software systems?}

Examining the resolution time of PTM-related issues is essential to quantify their impact. Building on RQ1, this research question examines whether PTM-related issues take longer to be resolved than non-PTM issues, inspired by \cite{Lai2024}. Investigating these differences helps determine if PTM-specific adaptations of software engineering best practices are needed. This question also explores whether different categories of PTM-related challenges influence resolution time.

% As whether the categories of PTM-related issues impact resolution time is unknown, the difference across PTM-related themes is also investigated.

