% PTMs introduce a distinct set of challenges when integrated into software projects, such as such as model compatibility, fine-tuning difficulties, dependencies, documentation, and performance bottlenecks. Understanding these challenges is crucial for improving the integration process and ensuring long-term maintenance of PTM-based systems. This research question seeks to identify and analyze the difficulties developers encounter due to incorporating PTMs in their software project. To address this, we employ qualitative analysis to develop a taxonomy of these challenges.


\subsection{Data Collection and Pre-processing}
For this study, we utilized the PeaTMOSS dataset \cite{Jiang2024}, which contains 28,575 GitHub projects that reuse 281,638 PTMs from Hugging Face and PyTorch Hub. The data was collected as of July 10, 2023. However, it is possible that these GitHub projects may not be software projects (e.g., PTM repositories). Since our goal is to understand the PTM-related issues in the downstream software projects that reuse PTMs, we conduct the following steps to curate the dataset.

