    % \end{itemize}    
We define a metric space $(P',|\cdot|)$ with $P'=P \cup \{u,v\}$ by the following distances:
  \begin{itemize}
         \item $|pq|=w(p,q)+15M$, for $\{p,q\}\in E$,
         \item $|pq|=14M+15M=29M$, for $\{p,q\}\notin E$, and
        \item $|up|=|vp|=|vu|=15M+15M=30M$ for $p\in P$.
    \end{itemize}   

  So, for each missing edge of a complete graph on $P$, we assign its weight to be $14M$. Therefore, we obtain a metric with distances in $\left[7M,14M\right]$.
  Then, we add the points $u$ and $v$ with distance $15M$ to each point in $p\in P$. 
 To  preserve the metric, we increase the distance of every tuple by $15M$.
 This construction is visualised in \cref{fig:APSP-hardness-sketch}.

