Finally, as noted in~\cite{ESA23}, in many applications some bi-directed edges might be allowed. This opens up a whole new set of questions on the trade-off between dilation and the number of bi-directed edges. Since this is a generalisation of the oriented case, both of our hardness results also apply to such models.

