Each test vector \( \boldsymbol{y}_i \) is used to evaluate neighborhood preservation in the reduced space. We first compute the \( k \)-nearest neighbors of \( \boldsymbol{y}_i \) in the original space \( X \), and then compare this neighborhood with the \( k \)-nearest neighbors of \( f(\boldsymbol{y}_i) \) in the reduced set \( X' \). This comparison provides the basis for our quantitative evaluation of local structure preservation under dimensionality reduction.


