We do not use reinforcement learning (RL)\cite{wang2021rlschert} or graph neural networks (GNNs)~\cite{adimora2024gnn} in this work, as these methods typically optimize for a single scalar objective (e.g., reward or cost) and require extensive environment tuning and retraining for new objective trade-offs. In contrast, our LLM-based ReAct agent supports multi-objective reasoning in a flexible, interpretable way (without retraining) by conditioning on natural language prompts that describe scheduling goals for jobs.


